# The cut: all of src/e2e/. Each file names only the identity (pod-identity),
# the resumable layer and its handover (pod-session), the answer of a peer
# (pod-session), the names and the safe text (pod-core): no file names
# serve/, reverse/, the CLI or another module of podssh. ask.rs is the word
# of the proof, which handshake.rs reads and checks. person.rs is the gate
# of a node's person: the question goes to the caller's Asker, so the crate
# has no terminal; ends.rs asks it after the door. The process globals of
# net.rs (the installed documents) and of hold/mod.rs (the registry of the
# holds) become values of the caller: Node::docs and Node::holds.
# Of the tests: e2e.rs, e2e_faults.rs, e2e_net.rs, e2e_harness/mod.rs, and
# routes.rs and person.rs (they run src/e2e/ alone over the harness). Of
# session_handover.rs the test
# a_session_of_the_channel_goes_on_across_a_handover_with_its_keys_and_nonces
# (pod-session left it for this crate). e2e_layered.rs stays in podssh until
# pod-relay: it runs reverse::{Layered, E2e, Handler}. podssh keeps a copy of
# e2e_harness/mod.rs for its tests that stay (grant.rs, quick_exit.rs,
# e2e_layered.rs).
